/-!
# A certified sixty-coset cover for Gebhardt's bottom subgroup

The five relations of Gebhardt, Experimental Mathematics 9 (2000),
333–338, Section 3B, give a cover of the two-generator group by sixty
right cosets of the cyclic subgroup generated by `a`. This proof replays
an untrusted Todd–Coxeter enumeration using actual subgroup-witness
identities. It includes the four coincidences among 64 immutable words.
Every deduction uses a defining word, a subgroup loop, a rotated defining
relator, reversal, or composition with free reduction.

The reproducible producer is in `GebhardtLocalBaseCertificate/source/`.
Neither a permutation quotient nor an external computation is a premise.
-/

namespace Lyons.Gebhardt.BaseCertificate
open Subgroup.CosetWordCertificate

set_option maxRecDepth 8192

/-- Signed forms of the five literal bottom-group relations, with `false = a`
and `true = b`. The commutator convention is `x⁻¹*y⁻¹*x*y`. -/
@[expose] public def relatorWord (r : Fin 5) : Word Bool :=
  (match r.val with
  | 0 => [(false, true), (false, true), (false, true), (false, true), (false, true), (false, true), (false, true), (false, true)]
  | 1 => [(true, true), (true, true), (true, true), (true, true), (true, true)]
  | 2 => [(false, true), (true, true), (false, true), (true, true), (false, true), (true, true), (false, true), (true, true)]
  | 3 => [(false, false), (false, false), (true, false), (false, true), (false, true), (true, true)]
  | 4 => [(false, false), (true, false), (false, true), (true, true), (false, false), (true, false), (false, true), (true, true), (false, false), (true, false), (false, true), (true, true)]
  | _ => [])

